# Trivy suppressions for the worker image scan (.github/workflows/ci.yaml).
# Each entry documents a vulnerability we have evaluated and accepted; the
# bare CVE id on its own line is what actively suppresses it. Review on each
# worker-image bump and delete entries whose fix has shipped.

# CVE-2026-34040 - Docker SDK Moby daemon authz-bypass (v29.3.1 fixes);
# the chat service uses the Docker *client* only, against a trusted local
# daemon; govulncheck reports no finding. v28->v29 major bump pending
# Dependabot review.
CVE-2026-34040

# --- The apt-installed GitHub CLI (/usr/bin/gh, latest release v2.97.0) is a
# prebuilt upstream binary compiled with Go 1.26.5; these are stdlib and
# vendored x/net findings in that embedded toolchain, fixed in Go 1.26.6.
# Everything this repo compiles is already on 1.26.6 (builder image, in-image
# toolchain, chat binary - all scan clean); only GitHub's release pipeline can
# rebuild gh. Inside the worker container repo-controlled code already executes
# arbitrary bash, so these DoS/parsing issues add no marginal attack surface.
# Clears when apt pulls a gh release built on Go >= 1.26.6. (The previous entry
# here, CVE-2026-39822 against a Go 1.26.4 gh, cleared when v2.97.0 shipped.)
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-46600
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862

# CVE-2026-14257 / CVE-2026-69152 - npm-bundled brace-expansion 5.0.7 DoS via
# glob brace expansion (5.0.8 and 5.0.9 fix); the single-tenant worker only
# expands globs npm generates itself. npm 11.19.0 (the newest npm that
# supports Node 25) still bundles 5.0.7; clears when an npm upgrade pulls in
# >= 5.0.9.
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152

# CVE-2026-69192 - npm-bundled ip-address 10.2.0 SSRF-shaped parse
# inconsistency (10.3.1 fixes), on npm's socks-proxy path which the worker
# does not configure. npm 11.19.0 still bundles 10.2.0; clears when an npm
# upgrade pulls in >= 10.3.1.
CVE-2026-69192

# --- The uv-managed CPython (/opt/python) bundles pip, whose _vendor tree pins
# msgpack==1.1.2 and setuptools==70.3.0 (pip/_vendor/vendor.txt - Trivy reads
# the pins as installed packages). GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 (msgpack Unpacker-reuse
# out-of-bounds read, fixed in 1.2.1) touches only pip's deserialization of its
# own local HTTP cache. CVE-2025-47273 (setuptools PackageIndex path traversal,
# fixed in 78.1.1) lives in package_index.py, which pip's vendored copy does not
# ship - only the pkg_resources subset of setuptools is vendored. The pins
# cannot be raised independently of pip, and the latest pip (26.2) still carries
# both - clears when a pip release re-vendors msgpack >= 1.2.1 and setuptools
# >= 78.1.1.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273

# CVE-2026-56852 - golang.org/x/text v0.36.0 inside the golangci-lint binary:
# DoS on invalid UTF-8 input to a lint binary running repo-controlled code
# that can already execute arbitrary bash. The latest golangci-lint release
# (v2.12.2) pins v0.36.0 and `go install pkg@version` cannot raise a module's
# own dependency pins; clears when a golangci-lint release requires x/text
# >= v0.39.0.
CVE-2026-56852

# --- util-linux 2.41-5 in the debian:trixie-slim base (bsdutils, libblkid1,
# libmount1, libsmartcols1, libuuid1, mount, util-linux and friends); the fix
# is 2.41.5-0+deb13u1. All four are in the SUID mount(8) program (TOCTOU and an
# integer overflow) - the worker never invokes mount and runs as the
# unprivileged user. The newest debian:trixie-slim tag (2026-08-05) still ships
# 2.41-5, so no digest refresh clears this yet - clears when a trixie-slim
# digest carries deb13u1.
CVE-2026-53612
CVE-2026-53613
CVE-2026-53614
CVE-2026-53615

# --- golang.org/x/mod inside the gh (v0.38.0), gofumpt (v0.38.0) and
# golangci-lint (v0.35.0) binaries; the fix is v0.40.0. Both CVEs are
# sumdb-related module-content forgery (CVE-2026-56864: malicious GOSUMDB
# serves arbitrary module content; CVE-2026-56865: malicious GOPROXY forges
# up to two sumdb entries). These tools run repo-controlled code that can
# already execute arbitrary bash, so they add no marginal attack surface. The
# latest releases (gh v2.97.0, gofumpt v0.11.0, golangci-lint v2.12.2) pin the
# affected versions and `go install pkg@version` cannot raise a module's own
# dependency pins - clears when those releases require x/mod >= v0.40.0. Same
# entries as contextmatrix-agent.
CVE-2026-56864
CVE-2026-56865

# --- The bundled npm CLI ships tar 7.5.19
# (/usr/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/tar); the fix is 7.5.21. DoS via a
# crafted long-path tar archive - inside the npm CLI the only archives tar
# reads are registry tarballs npm fetches itself on the single-tenant worker.
# npm's own transitive dependency: 11.19.0 (the newest npm that supports
# Node 25) and 12.0.2 both still bundle 7.5.19 - clears when an npm release
# pulls in >= 7.5.21.
CVE-2026-73566
